6 783 438\\nId: 0922803333 ✼ Date of birth: 30-10-1999\\nEducation\\nBachelor’s Degree in Chemistry Yachay Tech University\\nBachelor’s Degree Program September 2018 – May 2025\\nHigh School Diploma in Sciences (International Baccalaureate) Unidad Educativa Anc´on\\nHigh School Program May 2012 – March 2018\\nThesis Topic\\nSynthesis and Characterization of Cerium Oxide Nanoparticles Supported on Nano-Clays for their\\nPotential Catalytic Application. The study involved the chemical functionalization of clays via co-\\nprecipitation, purification of clay-based materials, and the use of a static Parr HPS 4790 series reactor\\nfor controlled material synthesis.\\nProfessional Experience & Extracurricular Activities\\nChemistry club instructor: Community-service pre-professional practicum April-June 2023\\nProject explanation: Unidad Educativa Fiscomisional Salesiana S´anchez y Cifuentes\\nDevelopment, guidance, advising, and training on the use of laboratory materials and chemical reagents\\nthrough the design and execution of demonstrative experiments for Second Baccalaureate students.\\nDuration 102 hours.\\nResearch assistant: Separation, purification and characterization of Ecuadorian clays as\\nprecursors of nanoclays for CO\\n2 \\ncapture and conversion July-September 2022\\nProject explanation: Urcuqu´ı, Imbabura\\nResearch assistant associated with the project “Use of Ecuadorian clays for CO\\n2 \\ncapture and conver-\\nsion,” focused on ferruginous clays for acid gas capture. Responsibilities included sample preparation,\\nchemical analysis, and physicochemical characterization of materials using FT-IR, XRD and TGA. Also\\nassisted the professor in practical teaching sessions, supporting students in the handling of characteri-\\nzation equipment (UV-Vis, FT-IR, XRD, chromatography). Duration 240 hours.\\nUndergraduate researcher: Synthesis and characterization of cerium oxide nanoparticles\\nsupported on nano-clays 2024-2025\\nProject explanation: Urcuqu´ı, I